# JavaScript Standards

## Conventions

- Vanilla JS only — no npm dependencies or external libraries
- Use `const` by default, `let` when reassignment needed, never `var`
- Named functions for module logic; arrow functions for callbacks
- Chrome APIs use callback style (matching existing codebase)

## Content Script

```javascript
// ✅ Required pattern
(function () {
  if (window.__linkedinEmailCollectorInitialized) return;
  window.__linkedinEmailCollectorInitialized = true;
  // ...
})();
```

## Async Messages

```javascript
// ✅ Return true for async sendResponse
chrome.runtime.onMessage.addListener((request, sender, sendResponse) => {
  if (request.action === "myAction") {
    doWork().then((result) => sendResponse(result));
    return true;
  }
});
```

## Error Handling

- Check `chrome.runtime.lastError` after `sendMessage`, `executeScript`, `tabs.get`
- Wrap DOM operations in try/catch when elements may be missing
- User-facing errors via `updateStatus()` in popup, not `alert()`
